    "reasoning": "All 16 final worked-solution answers agree with the mathematics and the selected current choices. There is one authored source error: q-113369 opens with y=-5/x+1, although its question, final transformation, and final graph correctly use y=-5/x+2. This typo does not change the correct selection. For the perpendicular-line questions, taking negative reciprocal slopes and imposing the given point or intercept gives the listed equations. Secant has period 2\\pi, is even, has no zeros, and has range (-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty); these facts establish the secant answers. The graph of -6/x has asymptotes x=0 and y=0 and passes through (-1,6) and (1,-6). The graph of -5/x+2 has asymptotes x=0 and y=2 and passes through (-1,7) and (1,-3). Distances to vertical lines are horizontal coordinate differences, giving 2 and 5. The perpendicular through (0,2) to y=-x-4 is y=x+2; their intersection is (-3,-1). No submitted grades were supplied; every MA answer below is established by its own captured worked solution.",
